    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (AcceptanceBase is abstract). The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rules with a points system across the three layers that touch it:\n\n1. **`MembershipLevelResolver.java`** \u2014 Added `deriveMembershipPoints(...)`: starts at 0, `+2` email present, `+1` namesakeCount is 0, `+2` household of 3+, `+3` tenure over 365 days. Reworked `deriveMembershipLevel(...)` to bucket those points via a new `levelForPoints` helper: level 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+). Dropped the old cap-based constants.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `membershipPoints` mapping alongside the existing `membershipLevel` mapping so both fields are returned on the `OwnerDto`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `membershipPoints` schema property and updated `membershipLevel`'s description/constraints (now `minimum: 1, maximum: 4`, derived from points), so the generated DTO carries the new field.\n\nThe controller's audit log continues to use `deriveMembershipLevel` unchanged.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsPointsAndLevel` passes \u2014 a fresh owner with an email and unique name scores `membershipPoints=3` (2+1) \u2192 `membershipLevel=2`. Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
