    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you POST `/api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:166`), annotated `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` and `@Transactional`.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the handler body runs\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize` requires the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else `AccessDeniedException` \u2192 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`** (fails \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400):\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `email` (optional): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n   - Note: `@NotNull` allows whitespace-only strings through here; that gap is closed in Phase 1.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 `normalizeAndValidate(dto)` (validations + DTO mutations, in order)\n3. **Normalize address** (side-effect): trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE; null \u2192 `\"\"`.\n4. **`validateRequiredFields`**: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone must be non-blank (address checked *after* normalization) \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. **`validatePostcode`** (only if postcode present): if city maps to a known Region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), postcode must fall in that region's range \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n6. **Normalize telephone** (validation + side-effect): convert to E.164; must be 8\u201315 digits, correct national length for +61 (9) / +1 (10) \u2192 else `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). Normalized value written back to DTO.\n7. **`requireCityHasCapacity`**: count of existing owners in that city must be < 50 \u2192 else `OwnerCityFullException` (409).\n8. **`resolveRegistrationDate`** (validation + side-effect): default to today if absent; a *supplied* future date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400); then roll Sat/Sun forward to Monday, write back to DTO.\n9. **`requireDailyLimitNotReached`**: count of existing owners on that (adjusted) registration date must be < 100 \u2192 else `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (429).\n10. **Normalize email** (validation + side-effect): lower-case; disposable domains (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (400). Written back to DTO.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Map to entity\n11. **`ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)`** \u2014 MapStruct copy of normalized fields into a new `Owner`.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 `populateDerivedFields` (side-effects, in order)\n12. **`customerCode`** = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; hash of canonical telephone + lastName).\n13. **`namesakeCount`** = count of existing owners with same first+last name (snapshot before save).\n14. **`bulkSignupWarning`** = true if > 80 owners already registered that day.\n15. **`householdId`** = null if postcode blank, else hash of lastName + postcode.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Duplicate / household checks\n16. **`requireUniqueIdentity`**: identity key = `telephone|email|householdId`; if any existing owner matches \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (409).\n17. **`requireHouseholdNotDuplicate`**: skipped if `sharesHousehold=true` or no household; else if another owner shares the `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (409).\n18. **`flagPossibleDuplicate`** (soft flag, side-effect): sets `possibleDuplicate=false`; unless `sharesHousehold=true`/no postcode, scans for an owner with same lastName + postcode but different phone, and if found sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<id>`.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Persist and finish\n19. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 the only DB write (`ownerRepository.save`, itself `@Transactional`). No cascade (pets empty on create).\n20. **`populateHouseholdMemberCount`** (transient side-effect): sets `householdMemberCount` (1, or count sharing the household including the new owner).\n21. **Audit log** (side-effect): `AUDIT.info(\"owner created: ...\")` including a derived membership level. This is an SLF4J log line only \u2014 no Spring `ApplicationEvent` is published.\n22. **Build response**: map to `OwnerDto` (stamps `identityKey`), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes\n- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks or listeners** fire: `Owner`/`Person` have no `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`, no `@EntityListeners`, no auditing listener. All timestamps/derived fields are set explicitly in the controller as above.\n- The entity `Owner` carries its own Bean Validation annotations, but the controller enforces equivalent checks manually before saving.\n- All error responses come from `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (`@ControllerAdvice`) as RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` bodies.\n- Worth being aware of (not something you asked to change): the capacity, daily-limit, namesake, and duplicate checks all count in memory over `findAllOwners()` with no backing DB unique constraint, so they're subject to races under concurrent POSTs."
